SUMMARY:Deadline: Movies that Matter Festival 2027: Film Submissions
DESCRIPTION:Movies that Matter\, the human rights film festival in The Hagu
 e (19-27 March 2027)\, is open for 2027 submissions. The festival screens 
 poignant fiction films and revealing documentaries that stir debates about
  human rights\, sustainability and the fight against injustice\, and feeds
  several competitions: the Grand Jury Documentary Competition (eight docum
 entaries\, EUR 5\,000\, winner eligible for...\n\nOrganisation: Movies tha
 t Matter\nLocation: The Hague\, Netherlands (festival 19-27 March 2027)\; 
 submissions open worldwide\, attendance not required for submission.\nAwar
 d: Cash prizes: EUR 5\,000 Grand Jury Documentary award (winner also becom
 es eligible for consideration for the Academy Award for Best Documentary F
 eature)\, EUR 5\,000 Grand Jury Fiction award\, and EUR 1\,500 Shorts awar
 d\; further competitions (Activist Lens\, Justice Frame\, Dutch Focus\, Ed
 ucation Award\, Audience Award) publish no amounts. SUBMISSION FEE: EUR 25
  until 30 September 2026\, EUR 35 late fee 1 October to 1 November 2026\; 
 fee waivers only in very exceptional cases.\n\nMore: https://moviesthatmat
 ter.nl/en/festival/industry/film-submissions/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://moviesthatmatter.nl/en/festival/industry/film-submissions/?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands (festival 19-27 March 2027)\; submissions 
 open worldwide\, attendance not required for submission.
END:VEVENT
